{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"Yes. A scholarship reserved for Black students can be morally acceptable when it addresses documented disadvantage, expands access to education, or helps remedy past exclusion.\n\nThat does not make every such scholarship justified. Its fairness depends on the need it addresses, how well its eligibility rules serve that purpose, and the effects on other students. Race-conscious support can be defensible without treating race as a measure of anyone’s worth."}}
